          "message": "fix(commenting): put the hide toggle before the filter menu (#11135)\n\nThis PR swaps the two actions in the comments panel header so the hide\ncomments toggle sits to the left of the filter menu.\n\n### Before\n\n`CanvasCommentsSidebar` rendered `CommentsFilterMenu` (the \u22ee menu) first\nand `CommentsVisibilityToggle` (the eye) last.\n\n### After\n\nThe eye toggle comes first, and the \u22ee filter menu is now the rightmost\naction in the header.\n\n### Change type\n\n- [x] `improvement`\n\n### Test plan\n\n1. Open a file and open the comments panel.\n2. Check that the eye toggle is to the left of the \u22ee menu, and that both\nstill work.\n\n### Release notes\n\n- Move the comments filter menu to the right of the hide comments toggle\nin the comments panel header.\n\n### Code changes\n\n| Section   | LOC change |\n| --------- | ---------- |\n| Core code | +1 / -1    |\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
